From: Yury Klushin <digger@live.ru>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] uknc: add k7 string literal prefix

The uknc target uses a KOI7 console path where SO/SI switch the Russian
and Latin glyph sets.  The project had a TO_KOI7 macro for this, but the
macro expansion is necessarily large and expensive for the compiler to
parse.

Add a uknc-only k7"..." string literal prefix.  The preprocessor accepts
it only when the target config defines TARGET_UKNC_DEFAULTS, and the
literal is interpreted as an ordinary char array whose contents are the
UKNC KOI7 bytes.  Cyrillic letters are mapped like the existing helper:
uppercase and lowercase Russian letters use the UKNC KOI layout, Yo maps
to Ye, ASCII uses the Latin shift, and unrepresentable non-ASCII
characters become '?'.

